# What never reaches the build context.
#
# Mostly about size and cache hits: a host `node_modules` would be the largest
# thing in the context by an order of magnitude, and copying it in would
# invalidate the layer that exists to avoid reinstalling it.

# Installed in the build stage by `npm ci`, from the lockfile. A host copy is
# the wrong platform's binaries as often as not.
node_modules
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log

# Build output. Produced inside the image; a stale host copy being copied in
# and then overwritten is pure waste, and worse when the overwrite is partial.
dist
tmp
out-tsc
.angular

# Not the app.
.git
.gitignore
.github
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
coverage
.vscode
.idea
.editorconfig
.prettierrc
.DS_Store
